WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.507
I just love the idea of making a world.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.409
It's an art, but it's also a craft.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:13.980
I've always been interested in
history and politics and how that informs

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.149
what we do, how we think,
what we wear.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:21.021
Everything is interesting and informative
to what people wear or wore.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:22.722
My job is to

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:28.928
help translate the director
and the actor's vision for the character

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.331
and kind of help tell the story.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:37.070
And also help the audience understand
who the person is, where they are in time.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.639
There are the homages to

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.207
Wong Kar-wai
In the Mood for Love.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:45.211
But also references Michelle Yeoh,
the actress.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:49.282
She had suggested some brands that
she liked, and one of them was Elie Saab.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:52.452
They had graciously sent some
dresses for us to borrow.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:56.056
The one that we see is the one that
we thought worked the best for the scene.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.457
We did submerse a lot

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.426
of clothing in the water.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:03.596
We needed to be honest about what
happens when things

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.365
are in the water and how do they move.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.067
So we informed VFX.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.670
It wasn't VFX informing us,
it was the other way around.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.006
It started out as a concept of red.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.274
It was a work in progress

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:17.710
and it took us about six prototypes,
but eventually we narrowed it down.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.246
Everybody keeps on saying it's a
dress and it's not a dress.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.549
I call it a playsuit and it's shorts.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.983
The idea was that it was Nellie’s.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.518
She had very little money at the time.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.053
In my mind, she cobbled it together.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:31.057
If you have good costumes,
you should be able

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:35.795
to read more into it than just
that person is wearing a red shirt.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:39.099
You should be able to feel who the
person is and where you are.

